-- title:
--   Capped rational acceptance value semantics
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a state type, $u$ a Boolean tape, $T\in\mathbb N$ a trial cap, $\theta\in\mathbb Q$, $x,y\in A$ old and proposed states, and $b$ a starting bit position. Put $a=|\operatorname{num}(\theta)|$ and $v=\operatorname{den}(\theta)>0$. If $\theta\ge1$, return $(y,b)$. Otherwise run the capped uniform draw with denominator $v$; absence aborts, and a successful value $z$ and position $b'$ return
--   $$\operatorname{some}\bigl((\text{if }z<a\text{ then }y\text{ else }x),b'\bigr).$$
--   No nonnegativity hypothesis on $\theta$ is included. The absolute numerator is used even for negative ratios, so the definition alone does not assert acceptance probability $\min(1,\theta)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RationalAcceptanceSubkernel.lean#L16-L23

